C64 HANGMAN
===========

TITLE:     C64 Hangman
AUTHOR:    JDC
YEAR:      2026
VERSION:   @VERSION@
PLATFORM:  Commodore 64 (PAL and NTSC)
BUILT:     @DATE@ from git @GITHASH@


DESCRIPTION
-----------

C64 Hangman is the classic word-guessing game for the Commodore 64,
written from scratch in 6502 assembly language. Guess the hidden word
one letter at a time before the hangman is complete.

It has a title screen with big colour lettering and a SID jingle,
sound effects for every guess, and win and loss jingles. Words are
5 to 12 letters long: a handful of C64-themed words (COMMODORE,
KERNAL, DATASETTE ...) plus the most common English words.

Two versions are included. The normal version has @WORDS@ words.
The XL version packs @WORDS_XL@ words into the C64's memory by storing
each letter in 5 bits and using the RAM hidden under the BASIC ROM.


HOW TO PLAY
-----------

Objective: find the hidden word before you make six wrong guesses.

Controls (keyboard only, no joystick needed):

  Any key     start a game from the title screen
  A to Z      guess a letter
  Any key     after a round, play a new word

A right letter is filled in everywhere it appears in the word, with a
chime. A wrong letter is listed under MISSES, adds a piece to the man,
flashes the border and costs one of your six lives. Letters you have
already tried are ignored.

Scoring: WINS and LOSSES are counted for the session (up to 99 each).
When you lose, the word is shown.

Tips: start with common letters such as E, T, A, O, I, N and S. Keys
pressed while a sound is playing are ignored, so there is no need to
hurry. The same word never comes up twice in a row.


HOW TO LOAD
-----------

Real hardware (or any emulator), from the disk image @D64@:

  LOAD"*",8,1        loads HANGMAN (the normal version)
  RUN

  LOAD"HANGMAN XL",8,1
  RUN                loads the XL version

The .prg files can also be loaded on their own, with LOAD"name",8,1
and RUN. The -packed files are compressed and unpack themselves after
RUN. The unpacked files start with a BASIC line, SYS 2061.

VICE (x64sc), from a command line:

  x64sc -autostart @D64@
  x64sc -autostart hangman-xl-packed.prg

Or drag a .d64 or .prg file onto the VICE window to autostart it.

Cartridge: there is no cartridge (.crt) version.

The Internet Archive's in-browser emulator may be able to run the
disk image or a .prg file directly from this item's page.


