TECHNICAL NOTES
---------------

Built with ACME @ACME@, exomizer @EXOMIZER@ and VICE @VICE@ (c1541).

Memory: every .prg loads at $0801 (2049) and starts with a BASIC
SYS 2061 line. The normal version ends at $@END@, below the BASIC
ROM. The XL version switches the BASIC ROM out and ends at $@END_XL@,
below the I/O area at $D000.

How it works:

- Text mode only, drawn directly into screen and colour RAM. No
  sprites or raster interrupts; the KERNAL IRQ stays on and provides
  the 60 Hz jiffy clock used for timing.
- SID voices 1 and 2 play the sound effects and jingles through a
  small blocking player. Voice 3 runs as a muted noise generator and
  is the random number source.
- Each word is picked with a random number re-rolled until it is in
  range, so every word is equally likely. An index of every 32nd word
  keeps the lookup fast.
- Notes are tuned for PAL; on NTSC they play about 4% sharp at the
  same tempo.


BUILDING FROM SOURCE
--------------------

Source: https://github.com/jaydarkseed757/c64-hangman

Tools: ACME 0.97, exomizer 3.1, VICE (x64sc, c1541), GNU make, and
Python 3 (only to regenerate the word lists).

  make                    build/hangman.prg
  make xl                 build/hangman-xl.prg
  make crunch             both exomizer-packed .prg files
  make d64                build/hangman.d64 with both versions
  make run                build and run in x64sc
  make internet-archive   this package, in internet-archive/


